# Styling Guidelines - Tailwind CSS v4 with Shadcn

## Shadcn Variables Approach

### Primary Rule: Use Shadcn Variables

**✅ ALWAYS customize shadcn variables directly in `:root`:**

```css
:root {
  /* Customize existing shadcn variables for your theme */
  --background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2c3e50 0%, #34495e 50%, #95a5a6 100%);
  --foreground: #ffffff;
  --card: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
  --card-foreground: #ffffff;
  --primary: #ffffff;
  --primary-foreground: #2c3e50;
  --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  --input: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  --muted-foreground: #dfe6e9;
  --ring: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
}
```

**❌ NEVER create custom CSS variables for theming:**

```css
/* Wrong - Don't create custom variables */
--custom-glass-bg: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
--custom-glass-text: #ffffff;
--glass-button-bg: #ffffff;
```

### Color Usage in Components

**✅ Use shadcn semantic classes:**

```tsx
// Correct - Use shadcn semantic classes
<div className="bg-card text-card-foreground border-border" />
<button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/90" />
<input className="bg-input border-border text-foreground placeholder:text-muted-foreground" />
```

**❌ Don't use hardcoded colors or custom variables:**

```tsx
// Wrong - Hardcoded colors
<div className="text-[#ffffff] bg-[rgba(255,255,255,0.15)]" />

// Wrong - Custom variables
<div className="text-[var(--custom-glass-text)] bg-[var(--custom-glass-bg)]" />
```

## Available Shadcn Variables

### Layout & Background
- `bg-background` - Main background
- `text-foreground` - Main text color

### Card Components
- `bg-card` - Card background
- `text-card-foreground` - Card text
- `border-border` - Border color

### Interactive Elements
- `bg-primary` - Primary button/action background
- `text-primary-foreground` - Primary button text
- `bg-secondary` - Secondary elements
- `text-secondary-foreground` - Secondary text

### Form Elements
- `bg-input` - Input background
- `border-input` - Input borders (falls back to border)
- `placeholder:text-muted-foreground` - Placeholder text

### States & Effects
- `ring-ring` - Focus rings
- `bg-accent` - Hover/accent states
- `text-muted-foreground` - Muted text

## Theme Customization Process

1. **Identify the UI element type** (card, button, input, etc.)
2. **Find the corresponding shadcn variable** (--card, --primary, --input, etc.)
3. **Customize the variable value in `:root`**
4. **Use the semantic Tailwind class** (`bg-card`, `bg-primary`, etc.)

### Example: Glassmorphism Theme

```css
:root {
  /* Glassmorphism theme using shadcn variables */
  --background: linear-gradient(135deg, #2c3e50 0%, #34495e 50%, #95a5a6 100%);
  --card: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
  --primary: #ffffff;
  --input: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
}
```

```tsx
// Components automatically inherit glassmorphism styling
<Card className="backdrop-blur-[15px]">  {/* Uses --card variable */}
  <Button>Submit</Button>  {/* Uses --primary variable */}
  <Input />  {/* Uses --input and --border variables */}
</Card>
```

## Responsive Design Rules

1. **Never use fixed max-width pixels:**

   ```tsx
   // Wrong
   <div className="max-w-[1440px]" />

   // Correct
   <div className="container mx-auto" />
   ```

2. **Use responsive breakpoints:**
   - `sm:` - 640px and up
   - `md:` - 768px and up
   - `lg:` - 1024px and up
   - `xl:` - 1280px and up
   - `2xl:` - 1536px and up

3. **Container approach:**
   ```tsx
   <div className="container mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 lg:px-8" />
   ```

## TailwindCSS Best Practices

### Class Ordering

Always follow consistent class ordering for maintainability:

1. Layout (position, display, flex, grid)
2. Sizing (width, height, padding, margin)
3. Typography (font, text)
4. Colors (background, text, border) - **Use shadcn classes**
5. Effects (shadow, opacity, transform)
6. States (hover, focus, active)

```tsx
// Good - Using shadcn semantic classes
<div className="relative flex w-full h-24 px-4 py-2 text-lg font-bold text-card-foreground bg-card rounded shadow hover:bg-card/90" />

// Avoid random ordering and hardcoded colors
<div className="text-[#1a1a1a] px-4 relative bg-[#ffffff] w-full hover:bg-[#f5f5f5] flex rounded py-2 h-24 shadow font-bold text-lg" />
```

### Single Quotes Convention

Always use single quotes for className attributes:

```tsx
// Good
<div className='bg-card text-card-foreground' />

// Avoid
<div className="bg-card text-card-foreground" />
```
